<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.0 20120330//EN" "JATS-archivearticle1.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Int Soc Sports Nutr</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition</journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="epub">1550-2783</issn><publisher><publisher-name>BioMed Central</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">19374756</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2675513</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">1550-2783-6-10</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1550-2783-6-10</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Dietary supplement increases plasma norepinephrine, lipolysis, and metabolic rate in resistance trained men</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes" id="A1"><name><surname>Bloomer</surname><given-names>Richard J</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref><email>rbloomer@memphis.edu</email></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author" id="A2"><name><surname>Fisher-Wellman</surname><given-names>Kelsey H</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref><email>kfshrwll@memphis.edu</email></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author" id="A3"><name><surname>Hammond</surname><given-names>Kelley G</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref><email>kghmmond@memphis.edu</email></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author" id="A4"><name><surname>Schilling</surname><given-names>Brian K</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref><email>bschllng@memphis.edu</email></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author" id="A5"><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>Adrianna A</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref><email>aaweber@memphis.edu</email></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author" id="A6"><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>Bradford J</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref><email>dr.bradfordcole@cptg.net</email></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="I1"><label>1</label>Department of Health and Sport Sciences, University of Memphis, Memphis, TN, USA</aff><pub-date pub-type="collection"><year>2009</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>17</day><month>4</month><year>2009</year></pub-date><volume>6</volume><fpage>10</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>7</day><month>4</month><year>2009</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>17</day><month>4</month><year>2009</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9;2009 Bloomer et al; licensee BioMed Central Ltd.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2009</copyright-year><copyright-holder>Bloomer et al; licensee BioMed Central Ltd.</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0"><license-p>This is an Open Access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0">http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0</ext-link>), which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</license-p></license></permissions><self-uri xlink:href="http://www.jissn.com/content/6/1/10"/><related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" id="d31e6" vol="6" page="4" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="19175919" ext-link-type="pubmed"/><abstract><p>Correction to Richard J Bloomer, Kelsey H Fisher-Wellman, Kelley G Hammond, Brian K Schilling, Adrianna A Weber and Bradford J Cole: Dietary supplement increases plasma norepinephrine, lipolysis, and metabolic rate in resistance trained men. <italic>Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition </italic>2009, 6: 4</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><sec><title>Correction</title><p>Following publication of our recent article [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B1">1</xref>], we noticed an error in Figure 2 A. The units of measure on the y-axis should range from 0 to 100 pg ml<sup>-1 </sup>rather than 100&#x02013;240 pg ml<sup>-1 </sup>as stated in the original article.</p><p>The corrected Figure 2 is presented here (Figure <xref ref-type="fig" rid="F1">1</xref>). The results and conclusions of this article remain unchanged.</p><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p><bold>Plasma epinephrine (A) and norepinephrine (B) data for 10 men consuming Meltdown<sup>&#x000ae; </sup>and placebo in a randomized cross-over design</bold>. Data are mean &#x000b1; SEM. * Greater norepinephrine AUC for Meltdown<sup>&#x000ae; </sup>compared to placebo (p = 0.03).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1550-2783-6-10-1"/></fig></sec></body><back><ref-list><ref id="B1"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Bloomer</surname><given-names>R J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fisher-Wellman</surname><given-names>K H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hammond</surname><given-names>K G</given-names></name><name><surname>Schilling</surname><given-names>B K</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>A A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>B J</given-names></name><article-title>Dietary supplement increases plasma norepinephrine, lipolysis, and metabolic rate in resistance trained men</article-title><source>Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition</source><year>2009</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>4</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19175919</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1550-2783-6-4</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>